course: dictionary
lesson: 8344
title: Rooftops
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A rooftop is the outside top surface of a roof. Read the context to find its meaning: «Many gulls have moved into towns and nest on flat rooftops, because cities have food and safe roofs away from foxes.» Gulls nest on flat rooftops, so a rooftop must be a place a bird can rest on top of a building. Ask: what word would fit here? Roof would fit, so a rooftop is the top of a roof.
explain: «Swifts scream over the rooftops catching flying ants.» Swifts fly above the rooftops, so the rooftops are the tops of buildings, seen from the sky. Try your meaning in the sentence: swifts scream over the tops of roofs catching ants. It still makes sense, so the meaning is right.
explain: The word can also describe something, as in «a rooftop garden», which is a garden on top of a roof. Some phrases use the word in a special way: «shout it from the rooftops» means tell everyone, loudly. Nobody is really shouting from a roof, so an idiom like this needs its own meaning.
fact: A rooftop is the outside top surface of a roof.
fact: «Rooftops» is the plural, which means more than one rooftop.
fact: Rooftop can also be an adjective, as in «a rooftop garden».
fact: Rooftop solar panels are panels fixed on roofs to catch sunlight.
fact: Never climb onto roofs, because falls are dangerous.
exercise: «Many gulls nest on flat rooftops in towns.» Where do the gulls nest? | In the sea | *On the outside top of a roof | Inside a shop | Under the ground
exercise: What is a rooftop garden? | A garden with a fence around it | A garden under the ground | A garden in the sea | *A garden on the top of a roof
exercise: «White storks nested on rooftops in England.» Find and copy the word that means more than one rooftop. | white | England | *rooftops | storks
test: What is the best meaning of rooftop? | A room at the bottom of a house | A window in the side of a house | A ladder that builders use | *The outside top surface of a roof
test: Jayden says, «Never climb onto a rooftop.» Why is this good advice? | Because roofs are always wet | Because roofs are too small to stand on | *Because falls from roofs are dangerous | Because birds will peck you
exam: What does «shout it from the rooftops» mean? | Sing a song | Climb onto a roof | Keep it a secret | *Tell everyone, loudly
